# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KLEOS Models .gitignore
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. The rules below are a safety net, not a substitute
# for judgement. Before committing, run:
#
#     python scripts/check_no_private_data.py .
#
# See SECURITY.md and docs/privacy.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- data/ is DENY-BY-DEFAULT ----------------------------------------------
#
# Everything under data/ is ignored unless explicitly allowed below.
#
# This is an allowlist on purpose. A blocklist ("ignore data/raw/, ignore
# *.jsonl") only blocks the filenames someone thought of in advance — drop a
# real export in as data/my_export.jsonl or data/memories.json and it sails
# straight into a public commit. Deny-by-default means a new file has to be
# *deliberately* permitted before it can ever be published.
#
# Real KLEOS training data belongs in the separate PRIVATE repository and is
# consumed by path, never copied here:
#
#     python scripts/train.py --config <config> --dataset /path/to/private/dataset
#
data/*

# The three things that ARE safe to publish.
# NOTE: comments must be on their own line. Git does not support trailing
# comments in .gitignore — "!data/schema/  # note" is a literal pattern that
# matches nothing, which silently un-ignores nothing at all.
!data/README.md
# JSON Schema: the data contract. Describes shape, contains no data.
!data/schema/
# Synthetic development fixtures. Generated, contain no real data.
!data/examples/

# Keep the empty working directories without admitting their contents.
!data/raw/
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/processed/
data/processed/*
!data/processed/.gitkeep

# Dataset artifacts anywhere else in the tree (a private export mounted or
# copied in, a Colab download, a sibling `dataset/` directory).
**/train.jsonl
**/validation.jsonl
**/test.jsonl
!data/examples/*.jsonl
!tests/fixtures/*.jsonl

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
credentials.json
service-account*.json
.hf_token
.huggingface/

# --- Training artifacts ----------------------------------------------------
# `outputs/*` rather than `outputs/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so "outputs/" followed by "!outputs/.gitkeep" would
# silently drop the .gitkeep and the directory would vanish from the repo.
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep
checkpoints/
runs/
wandb/
reports/
mlruns/
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.gguf
*.ckpt

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# --- Tooling ---------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# --- Notebooks -------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Editors / OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

#Mac OS
.DS_Store

# Local agent notes
claude.md
CLAUDE.md